# Personal Persona AI Chat - Environment Configuration Example
#
# The persona backend is now configured as a WORKER SECRET, not a VITE_ var.
# Vite inlines every VITE_* value into the shipped JS bundle, which would publish
# the upstream URL (and any key) to every visitor. The browser now always calls
# the worker's own /api/chat, and the worker proxies upstream.
#
# Set these with wrangler instead of putting them in .env:
#
#   npx wrangler secret put PERSONA_API_URL
#     Base URL:            https://api.yourdomain.com   (worker appends /api/chat)
#     or full endpoint:    https://api.yourdomain.com/api/chat
#
#   npx wrangler secret put PERSONA_API_KEY     # optional bearer token for upstream
#
# For local development, put the same values in a gitignored `.dev.vars` file at
# the repo root so `wrangler dev` picks them up:
#
#   PERSONA_API_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com
#   PERSONA_API_KEY=your_optional_token
#
# With no PERSONA_API_URL set, /api/chat returns a canned Indonesian reply.
#
# This file currently declares no client-side vars. If you add one, remember it
# will be public in the bundle.
